  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 oPt Emergency Appeal - West Bank - Protection</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNRWA will continue documenting protection threats and potential violations of International Humanitarian and Human Rights Law, including grave violations against children, while leading civil-military coordination and engaging authorities on protection and access issues. Support for vulnerable groups - women, children, and persons with disabilities - will be scaled up through community-based organizations (CBOs), which will help identify and respond to risks, establish gender-sensitive and child-friendly safe spaces, strengthen GBV referral mechanisms, support rehabilitation, provide assistive devices, and foster community engagement. UNRWA will deliver cash-for-protection to 600 families facing urgent protection needs and support 330 persons with disabilities through specialized mobility, hearing, vision and communication tools. The overall emergency response will apply gender, age, and disability-sensitive programming, integrate PSEA, and strengthen accountability to affected populations through enhanced hotline management, personnel training, and regular assessments of UNRWA facilities.</narrative>
  </description>
